NNAAMMEE
       prlimit - get and set process resource limits

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       pprrlliimmiitt [options] [----rreessoouurrccee[=_l_i_m_i_t_s]] [----ppiidd _P_I_D]

       pprrlliimmiitt [options] [----rreessoouurrccee[=_l_i_m_i_t_s]] _c_o_m_m_a_n_d [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Given a process ID and one or more resources, pprrlliimmiitt tries to retrieve
       and/or modify the limits.

       When _c_o_m_m_a_n_d is given, pprrlliimmiitt will run this command with the given
       arguments.

       The _l_i_m_i_t_s parameter is composed of a soft and a hard value, separated
       by a colon (:), in order to modify the existing values. If no _l_i_m_i_t_s
       are given, pprrlliimmiitt will display the current values. If one of the
       values is not given, then the existing one will be used. To specify the
       unlimited or infinity limit (RRLLIIMM__IINNFFIINNIITTYY), the -1 or 'unlimited'
       string can be passed.

       Because of the nature of limits, the soft limit must be lower or equal
       to the high limit (also called the ceiling). To see all available
       resource limits, refer to the RREESSOOUURRCCEE OOPPTTIIOONNSS section.

       •   _s_o_f_t:_hard_ Specify both limits.

       •   _s_o_f_t: Specify only the soft limit.

       •   :_h_a_r_d Specify only the hard limit.

       •   _v_a_l_u_e Specify both limits to the same value.

